'''Trinity Southwest University''' ('''TSU''') is an [[evangelical Christian]] institution of [[higher education]] with an office in [[Albuquerque, New Mexico]]. Principally a theological school that encompasses both the [[Bible college]] and [[theological seminary]] concepts of Christian education, it offers [[distance education]] programs and degrees in biblical studies, theological studies, archaeology and biblical history, biblical counseling, biblical representational research, and university studies.

==History==
TSU was founded as '''Southwest Biblical Seminary''' in [[Tulsa, Oklahoma]], where it provided Bible-oriented education for local students. In 1989 it relocated to Albuquerque, New Mexico. According to TSU, in 1990 it began an official association with "an internationally-known Bible college and seminary" (not identified), but it became an independent institution of higher education in 2001.<ref>{{citation|url=http://trinitysouthwest.com/history/ |title=History|publisher= Trinity Southwest University|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20101211104816/https://trinitysouthwest.com/history/|archivedate=December 11, 2010| accessdate=March 10, 2012}}</ref>

Most TSU students enroll in distance education. As of 2007 the typical student was an adult between 40 and 49 years old. At that time, the school occupied a former church in Albuquerque.<ref name=ABQ2007>{{citation |url=http://www.abqjournal.com/biz/264811business11-26-07.htm |title=Consolidation, a Name, and a School |author=Richard Metcalf |newspaper=Albuquerque Journal |date=November 26, 2007|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20131219050237/http://www.abqjournal.com/biz/264811business11-26-07.htm|archivedate=December 19, 2013}}</ref> As of October 2021 its location was described as "a strip mall in Albuquerque."<ref name=RetractionWatch/>

==Doctrine==
TSU is [[evangelical Christian]] in its orientation; it calls itself "trans-denominational". The school holds that biblical scripture, specifically "the ancient Hebrew Tanakh and the New Testament", is "the only written, divinely inspired representation of reality given by God to humankind, speaking with absolute and authority in all matters upon which it touches."<ref>{{cite web |title=About |url=https://trinitysouthwest.com/about-tsu/#doctrinal |website=Trinity Southwest University |access-date=16 July 2022}}</ref>

==Affiliations and accreditation status==
TSU is not [[Educational accreditation|accredited]] by any accreditor recognized by the [[United States Department of Education]]. The institution's position is that "any governmental association or oversight ... is inappropriate for a [[faith-based organization]] or institution, and constitutes a fundamental violation of church/state separation".<ref name=TSUaffiliations>{{citation |url=http://trinitysouthwest.com/affiliations/ |title=Affiliations| publisher=Trinity Southwest University |accessdate=March 10, 2012}}</ref> It currently operates in New Mexico under a religious exemption authorized by state law. TSU is a member of the [[Association of Christian Schools International]].<ref name=TSUaffiliations/>

